  "findings": [
    "eSIMs are keyed by order_id: activation_event has no esim_id. expiration_date_eSIM_v2 carries order_id, plan end date and ICCID, so plan_end_at per order is available from Klaviyo.",
    "Join key between hly_order_confirmed (order_number) and activation_event / expiration_date_eSIM_v2 (order_id, UUID) is unverified; until confirmed, pre-trip orders without an activation may not join.",
    "Country names are English names (activation_country) and SKU slugs (parent_sku 'esim-<country>'); nba/countries.py maps them to ISO-2.",
    "Only 8 of 50 recently updated profiles have external_id, in two formats; the service addresses profiles by Klaviyo profile id.",
    "hly_always_on_consumption_threshold.percentage is a string.",
    "hly_order_confirmed carries name, phone, email, billing and shipping address: the ingest reads only order_number, items and destination_localized, and verification never samples it. Flag to the data/privacy owner.",
    "No Intercom metrics in Klaviyo: CARE_OPEN and care_this_trip must come from Intercom or the warehouse.",
    "Daily usage is not in Klaviyo (gap 2): usage_daily comes from the warehouse."
  ]
